  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The real phone",
      "items": [
        "USB: scripts/usb.sh runs adb reverse tcp:8782, so the page is http://localhost:8782 on the phone, a secure page for camera and motion without a certificate (usb.sh 9–16). Over Wi-Fi it needs the bridge's https and its key instead.",
        "face.js opens one WebSocket to /ws and reconnects; code 4000 (another phone took over) stays quiet (face.js 447–460). The page reports its screen as keys and numbers every change and every 5 s (omi.js 347–367).",
        "phone_health speaks adb's own protocol to the adb server already on the host (shell, a DevTools forward), so the container needs no adb of its own, whose version would kill the host's server and the USB link (phone_health.py 21–88)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "The Webots twin",
      "items": [
        "--bridge: the twin is the phone. It connects to /ws like the page; the bridge cannot tell them apart, so ROS sees the same topics. It still opens /ws/mirror for the props (atl_phone_twin.py 875–879).",
        "--mirror: the real phone is in charge. The twin draws what the bridge sends the phone and the phone's screen report, and sends nothing but hello (atl_phone_twin.py 185–194, 390–407).",
        "Both run as extern controllers of the Webots on the host (tcp :1240/PH5v0001; the Thymio twin is atl-bot-thymio's). The robot's stack (Pi box, riser, clamp) is AtlOmiStack in the Thymio's bodySlot; the phone rides on it (AtlOmiStack.proto 5–11)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Gates",
      "items": [
        "/ws and /ws/mirror refuse a foreign Origin and a wrong key (hmac); /ws/mirror without a key answers this computer only (wsserver.py 322–330).",
        "/api/* answers loopback only (wsserver.py 343–352): the setup page, its props and its phone card work from the bridge's computer.",
        "A shown frame goes to loopback mirrors only (wsserver.py 225–231), so with the bridge on the Pi a PC over Wi-Fi gets no pictures."
      ]
    }
  ]
